  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "7 v 5 – get back and defend",
  "description": "Play on the whole rink, split into thirds with cones along the boards. Blue attack with six outfield players and a keeper. Red defend with a keeper and four players: two defenders in their own third and two midfielders in the middle third, where they defend at full intensity. Offside applies.\n\nWhen blue get into their last third, the two red midfielders must skate back, get goal-side and help protect the goal. If red win the ball they counter against blue's goal, and blue try to win it back straight away. A ball over the end line gives a corner or a goal throw, as in a match.\n\nProgression: play 7 v 7 with one unit in each third. When a team gets into its last third, the opponents may drop one third – midfield into their own third and forwards into the middle. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Midfielders: as soon as the ball passes you, skate back on the inside, between the ball and the goal."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The nearest defender presses the ball carrier out towards the boards; the others cover the space in front of goal."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "The keeper moves with the ball and organises the defence by talking."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "When you win the ball: look forward at once – the opponents have many players high up."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "phase": "main",
  "difficulty": 3,
  "focus": [
    "defence",
    "positioning",
    "transition"
  ],
  "durationMinutes": 25,
  "minPlayers": 12,
